Azure Virtual Networking.

Azure Virtual Network (VNet) allows Azure resources to communicate securely with each other, the internet, and on-premises networks.

Key Concepts:

Virtual Network (VNet)
A private network in Azure (like your own data center network)

Subnets
Divide a VNet into smaller sections for organization and security

IP Addressing
Each resource gets a private IP inside the VNet

Connectivity Options:
                          Internet
                          Resources can communicate with external networks

                          VPN Gateway
                          Secure connection between Azure and on-premises networks over the internet

                          ExpressRoute
                          Private, high-speed connection to Azure (not over the internet)

                          VNet Peering
                          Connect two VNets directly
Security Features:
                  Network Security Groups (NSGs)
                  Control inbound and outbound traffic (like a firewall)

                  Azure Firewall
                  Managed, centralized network security service

Use Cases:
          Isolate and secure applications
          Connect cloud and on-prem environments
          Control traffic between resources
